<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-WORLD CUP AFRICAN ZONE RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-WORLD CUP AFRICAN ZONE RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results from World</p>
<p>Cup African zone qualifiers played at the weekend:</p>
<p>Group 1</p>
<p>In Lagos: Nigeria 3 Kenya 0 (halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Sunday Oliseh 12, Emmanuel Amunike 43, Wilson Oruma</p>
<p>81</p>
<p>Attendance: 50,000</p>
<p>In Conakry: Guinea 3 Burkina Faso 1 (2-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Guinea - Fode Camara 10 pen, Camille Palenfou 24 own goal,</p>
<p>Soulaymane Oulare 56</p>
<p>Burkina Faso - Mamadou Zongo 9</p>
<p>    Standings   P  W  D  L   F  A Pts</p>
<p> Nigeria	  5  4  1  0  10  3  13</p>
<p> Guinea	   5  3  0  2   9  5   9</p>
<p> Kenya	    5  2  1  2   7 10   7</p>
<p> Burkina Faso   5  0  0  5   5 13   0</p>
<p>Nigeria qualify</p>
<p>Remaining matches: Aug 17 - Guinea v Nigeria, Conakry</p>
<p>Burkina Faso v Kenya, Ouagadougou</p>
<p>Group 2</p>
<p>In Cairo: Egypt 0 Tunisia 0</p>
<p>In Monrovia: Liberia 1 Namibia 2 (1-1)</p>
<p>Liberia - Prince Daye 7</p>
<p>Namibia - Eliphas Shivute 36, Gervatius Uri Khob 80</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p> Tunisia	  5  4  1  0   6   1  13</p>
<p> Egypt	    5  2  1  1  10   5   7</p>
<p> Liberia	  5  1  1  3   2   5   4</p>
<p> Namibia	  5  1  1  3   6  13   4</p>
<p>Tunisia qualify</p>
<p>Remaining matches: August 16 - Tunisia v Namibia, Tunis,</p>
<p>August 17 - Egypt v Liberia, Cairo</p>
<p>Group 3</p>
<p>In Johannesburg: South Africa 3 Zambia 0 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Helman Mkhalele 9, Phil Masinga 16, Mark Williams</p>
<p>74</p>
<p>Attendance: 70,000</p>
<p>In Pointe Noire: Congo 1 Democratic Republic of Congo</p>
<p>(formerly Zaire) 0</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p> South Africa	 5  3  1  1  6  3  10</p>
<p> Congo		  5  3  1  1  5  4  10</p>
<p> Zambia		 5  1  2  2  5  6   5</p>
<p> Dem Rep of Congo   5  0  2  3  4  7   2</p>
<p>Remaining matches: August 17 - South Africa v Congo,</p>
<p>Johannesburg, Zambia v DR Congo, Lusaka</p>
<p>Group 4</p>
<p>In Luanda: Angola 1 Cameroon 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Angola - Akwa 55</p>
<p>Cameroon - Patrick Mboma 54</p>
<p>Attendance: 60,000</p>
<p>In Lome: Togo 2 Zimbabwe 1 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Togo - Bachirou Salou 8, 20</p>
<p>Zimbabwe - Vitalis Takawira 71 pen</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p> Cameroon     5  3  2  0  8   3  11</p>
<p> Angola	 5  2  3  0  6   3   9</p>
<p> Zimbabwe     5  1  1  3  5   5   4</p>
<p> Togo	   5  1  0  4  5  13   3</p>
